  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough next Monday...\n\nSatellite imagery shows the departing upper low over southern\nManitoba and a flatter W-NW flow over the northern Rockies. There\nis an upstream shortwave along the BC coast that will be a player\nfor us later this week. Winds are decreasing and will shift to \neasterly today. Overall it will be a tranquil day with high temps \nin the upper 60s to lower 70s (after a chilly start), and much \nless wind than Monday. There is also a low risk (<15%) of fog over\nour north and east early today, as post-frontal dew points are \nclose to expected morning lows, but a west wind persisting beyond \nsunrise may prevent fog from developing despite the shrinking dew \npoint depressions.\n\nA weaker splitting shortwave from the NW will glance thru northern\nMT tonight into Wednesday. This looks mostly dry but another \nCanadian front will sag into the area reinforcing the below normal\ntemps for another day. Temps should climb into the 70s across the\narea Thursday.\n\nAforementioned BC wave will eventually evolve into a cut off low \nover OR/CA/NV by Wednesday. This feature will then track slowly \neastward, within a region of above normal heights, providing \nascent for shower activity and allowing for another surge of high \nplains moisture. In fact, pwats are expected to climb back over an\ninch over the east half of our forecast area by Friday. Greatest \npotential for showers seems to be late Thursday through Saturday. \nThunderstorms are possible Friday, with enough instability and \nslow storm motion to bring a risk of heavy rain, especially over \nthe east. Shear will likely be too low for a risk of severe \nstorms. Some showers could linger in the east into Sunday, but \nconsensus is for rising heights and drying from the west by then. \nLatest NBM probabilities show a 20-40% chance of 1+ inches of rain\nover the east Friday thru Saturday night. Regarding temperatures,\nthis is a seasonably warm system and snow levels will remain \nhigh, no lower than 10kft. Expect near to slightly cooler than \nnormal temps Friday/Saturday, then warming into early next week\nwith the ridging. Should see near 80F by next Monday, along with \ndry wx.\n\nJKL",
